# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true at system scope, which rewrites files
# to CRLF on checkout. This overrides it: LF in the index and in the working
# tree, on every platform.
#
# Line endings are load-bearing here. The corpus loader reads data/raw/*.txt
# positionally -- line 1 title, line 3 `Last updated:` -- and the sentence
# splitter collapses intra-paragraph newlines, so a stray \r would ride along on
# the end of every title, date and sentence and quietly poison extraction.
# setup.sh is run by sh, where CRLF breaks the shebang outright.
#
# text=auto still lets Git detect binaries and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
